Peter schrieb:
> As a chaotic Monk, if I attack and kill One-Eyed Sam will I lose either 
> accumulated protection or accumulated intrisics?

In fact, as a monk, one can take him on in melee, under three 
conditions.  I tried this out in wizard mode.  One has to quaff a potion 
of invulnerability, to be protected against the beheading attack of 
Thiefbane and to wear an amulet of drain resistance, otherwise a level 
will still be drained each time he hits you.  Moreover, to be able to 
fight at all, a ring of free action is necessary or Izzy the rhaumbusun 
has to be killed ahead of time.

This method is not very safe, however, because the fight tends to take 
long, so you may need several potions of invulnerability, more than you 
have, in fact.  And you tend to miss Sam often, due to his superior AC. 
  I managed to kill him the first time using ground slam.  The second time
took much longer, because my other techniques were not available.

So with good timing (all techniques available) and invulnerability, it 
is possible - provided you don't need more than the 12 turns that 
invulnerability protects you...
